@meta
id: 16-16
title: A window is just a view
chapter: 16
type: lesson
skills: split-window, buffer-switch, window-nav, buffer-list
par: 140
minutes: 7
vscode: split right, then use the file picker inside the new half
open: order.resolver.ts order.provider.ts

@brief
Put the two halves of the chapter together. A window shows a buffer,
and which buffer it shows is up to you: `:b name` inside a window
points that window at a different buffer and leaves every other window
alone. So `:sp` followed by `:b prov` gives you the resolver in one
window and the provider in the other, from two buffers that were
already loaded. `:sp name` was the same move for a file that was not.
`Ctrl-^` inside a window swaps that window, too. `:ls` after it shows
both buffers marked `a`, active, because both are on screen.

The ticket: cancelling an order needs a reason, and the schema already
sends one.

  1. `order.provider.ts`: `cancel(id: string)` becomes
     `cancel(id: string, reason: string)`, and the update values become
     `{ status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: reason }`.
  2. `order.resolver.ts`: `cancelOrder` passes it through:
     `this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id, args.reason)`.

Both files on screen, both edited, one `:wqa`.

@keys
| `:sp` then `:b prov` | split, then point the new window at the provider |
| `Ctrl-W j` | back down to the resolver's window |
| `Ctrl-^` | swap this window to its alternate buffer |
| `:ls` | `a` on every buffer that is in a window |

@hints
`:sp`, `:b prov`. The top window is now the provider and the bottom
one is still the resolver.
--
Provider: `/async cancel`, `f)`, `i`, type `, reason: string`, `Esc`.
Then `/CANCELLED'`, `f'`, `a`, type `, cancellationReason: reason`,
`Esc`.
--
`Ctrl-W j`. `/cancel(` finds the call and not the method name, `f)`,
`i`, `, args.reason`, `Esc`, `:wqa`.

@solution
    :sp<Enter>  :b prov<Enter>
    /async cancel<Enter>  f)  i , reason: string <Esc>
    /CANCELLED'<Enter>  f'  a , cancellationReason: reason <Esc>
    Ctrl-W j  /cancel(<Enter>  f)  i , args.reason <Esc>  :wqa<Enter>

About a hundred and twenty keystrokes; the layout cost twelve.

This is the model paying off. Buffers are what is loaded. Windows are
where you look. Any window can look at any buffer, and changing what a
window shows costs the same `:b` you would use with one window. Once
that is comfortable, `:sp name`, `:vs name`, `:sp` plus `:b`, and
`Ctrl-^` in a split are all the same idea wearing different keys, and
you stop thinking about which one to reach for.

VS Code has a version of this, but each editor group keeps its own tab
strip and the same file in two groups is two tabs that happen to agree.
Here it is one buffer, and the list does not care how many windows are
looking at it.

@start order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string; reason: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@expected order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string; reason: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id, args.reason);
  }
}

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string, reason: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: reason },
    });
  }
}
